Test result: `uv run pytest -q -m "not scenario"` — 3497 passed, 275 skipped,
5 deselected. No lint errors. Verified the live Lakebase engine resolves
`_sql_relation` and `_readable_table_id` to the same `physical_table_id`, so the
inherited SQL targets the correct union view.

Not done (phase B of the plan): the serverless Lakeflow job that would restore
PageRank, connected components and clustering coefficient at scale. This
environment has no `pyspark` and no JRE, so a Spark job cannot be executed or
tested locally — deferred pending a decision on whether to build it as
generated SQL (executable against SQLite in tests, like the phase A queries) or
the PySpark DataFrame API.
